1
00:00:00,992 --> 00:00:04,658
(hissing)

2
00:00:06,408 --> 00:00:11,784
(grunts)

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,241
(cackling)

4
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,784
(grunting)

5
00:00:36,785 --> 00:00:37,701
Haaaa!

6
00:00:37,785 --> 00:00:38,785
I've got you now!

7
00:00:47,035 --> 00:00:48,035
Huh?

8
00:00:48,868 --> 00:00:50,951
What's in that
blood he spits out?

9
00:00:51,035 --> 00:00:52,035
Some kind of poison?

10
00:00:53,284 --> 00:00:54,201
What's this?

11
00:00:54,284 --> 00:00:56,618
You're too strong.

12
00:00:56,701 --> 00:00:59,826
That's not very much fun at all.

13
00:01:01,242 --> 00:01:02,368
(warbling)

14
00:01:02,451 --> 00:01:05,659
Straw Doll Technique: Resonance!

15
00:01:07,077 --> 00:01:12,118
(upbeat music)

16
00:01:23,451 --> 00:01:24,451
(chittering)

17
00:01:24,493 --> 00:01:27,993
Tsk! How many of them are there?

18
00:01:28,077 --> 00:01:30,659
I guess we just keep going
like it's whack-a-mole, huh?

19
00:01:30,743 --> 00:01:31,785
Yeah.

20
00:01:31,868 --> 00:01:32,993
Keep going.

21
00:01:33,077 --> 00:01:35,159
Keep on exorcising them.

22
00:01:35,242 --> 00:01:36,910
We'll just wipe out all of them.

23
00:01:37,910 --> 00:01:39,451
It's unlikely to retaliate.

24
00:01:40,409 --> 00:01:42,159
I do get what you're saying...

25
00:01:42,242 --> 00:01:43,994
Its technique
covers a large area,

26
00:01:44,078 --> 00:01:47,202
so its main body doesn't
have much offense.

27
00:01:47,285 --> 00:01:49,078
I just said it's unlikely.

28
00:01:49,494 --> 00:01:51,452
All the things we
were worried about,

29
00:01:51,535 --> 00:01:55,994
its technique's range, the
number of victims, the barrier.

30
00:01:56,078 --> 00:01:58,369
All of those are subtracting
from its main body.

31
00:01:58,452 --> 00:02:00,827
So we're lucky.

32
00:02:00,911 --> 00:02:02,591
We'll be able to
exorcise it quickly, then.

33
00:02:03,869 --> 00:02:07,744
Which means, the real
problem comes after.

34
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:10,369
(gasp)

35
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:17,702
Kugisaki!

36
00:02:17,786 --> 00:02:19,327
I'll be fine.

37
00:02:20,452 --> 00:02:22,202
You just whack the mole!

38
00:02:25,494 --> 00:02:27,202
Damn it!

39
00:02:27,285 --> 00:02:28,994
She keeps getting
sucked into things!

40
00:02:29,494 --> 00:02:33,036
But what was that just now?

41
00:02:33,119 --> 00:02:34,119
The mole?

42
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,036
That earlier one?

43
00:02:36,119 --> 00:02:37,786
No, it's neither!

44
00:02:39,452 --> 00:02:40,369
Kugisaki?

45
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:42,827
Oh, hey, it's my older brother!

46
00:02:42,911 --> 00:02:43,327
Huh?

47
00:02:43,410 --> 00:02:45,744
Me too, me too!

48
00:02:48,327 --> 00:02:49,327
Huh?

49
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:52,160
It took off!

50
00:02:52,202 --> 00:02:53,453
Should I just let it go?

51
00:02:53,536 --> 00:02:55,286
No, go after it!

52
00:02:55,370 --> 00:02:58,578
Kugisaki and that thing
both went outside the barrier!

53
00:02:58,661 --> 00:03:00,912
She might be going
up against something

54
00:03:00,995 --> 00:03:03,079
even more dangerous
than we assumed!

55
00:03:03,161 --> 00:03:04,512
By contrast, things
here aren't so bad,

56
00:03:04,536 --> 00:03:06,370
I can handle this by myself!

57
00:03:06,453 --> 00:03:08,870
Save Kugisaki!

58
00:03:08,953 --> 00:03:09,953
Go!

59
00:03:10,037 --> 00:03:12,328
Alright but if
things go bad here

60
00:03:12,411 --> 00:03:14,828
then you follow us and get out!

61
00:03:21,495 --> 00:03:22,536
Why, you!

62
00:03:24,995 --> 00:03:26,037
Don't touch me!

63
00:03:32,203 --> 00:03:34,578
I didn't realize
you were a woman.

64
00:03:34,661 --> 00:03:35,787
But you are.

65
00:03:37,037 --> 00:03:38,037
Sorry.

66
00:03:38,453 --> 00:03:39,536
Yecchh.

67
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:43,370
We brothers were tasked
with a certain errand you see.

68
00:03:44,661 --> 00:03:46,578
But killing jujutsu sorcerers

69
00:03:46,661 --> 00:03:50,120
isn't part of that arrangement.

70
00:03:50,203 --> 00:03:53,286
So if you withdraw
we'll let you escape.

71
00:03:53,661 --> 00:03:56,453
Young woman.

72
00:03:56,536 --> 00:03:57,578
An errand?

73
00:03:57,661 --> 00:03:58,912
Hmm?

74
00:03:58,995 --> 00:04:01,203
I presumed you were
on the same errand.

75
00:04:02,371 --> 00:04:04,287
A cursed spirit
or a cursed user?

76
00:04:04,371 --> 00:04:04,871
Which is he?

77
00:04:04,954 --> 00:04:06,788
And what is that smell?

78
00:04:09,245 --> 00:04:11,162
(monster warbling)

79
00:04:14,287 --> 00:04:17,704
(grunting)

80
00:04:21,913 --> 00:04:22,913
Last one!

81
00:04:25,579 --> 00:04:26,454
You're not even trying.

82
00:04:26,537 --> 00:04:28,829
This is too easy.

83
00:04:32,579 --> 00:04:36,038
I told you you're
making this too easy!

84
00:04:40,245 --> 00:04:41,245
(sigh)

85
00:04:42,412 --> 00:04:43,704
And that's the last of them.

86
00:04:45,621 --> 00:04:49,162
So Tsumiki is safe
for the moment.

87
00:04:49,245 --> 00:04:51,080
Now, I just have to...

88
00:04:52,454 --> 00:04:55,454
(dripping)

89
00:04:59,537 --> 00:05:00,537
One survived?

90
00:05:01,829 --> 00:05:03,746
So that wasn't its
main body after all?

91
00:05:05,121 --> 00:05:07,204
The barrier hasn't
collapsed, either!

92
00:05:07,287 --> 00:05:08,329
What the?

93
00:05:10,579 --> 00:05:13,413
I shouldn't be trying
too hard to find logic

94
00:05:13,497 --> 00:05:15,747
in a cursed spirit's
behavioral patterns.

95
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:17,872
But the fact is,

96
00:05:17,955 --> 00:05:21,081
that question has been
nagging me this whole time.

97
00:05:24,288 --> 00:05:26,039
Why did it just
now start killing the

98
00:05:26,122 --> 00:05:27,122
humans it had marked?

99
00:05:27,497 --> 00:05:29,580
The first one was
killed back in June.

100
00:05:30,497 --> 00:05:31,580
And in June...

101
00:05:37,622 --> 00:05:39,538
Our only objective here

102
00:05:41,705 --> 00:05:44,622
is get Sukuna's finger and
return it to where it belongs.

103
00:05:44,705 --> 00:05:47,330
(evil cackle)

104
00:05:47,663 --> 00:05:50,914
(opening theme music)

105
00:05:52,872 --> 00:05:55,914
(singing in Japanese)

106
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:21,623
Some have a presence
that's too overwhelming.

107
00:07:21,706 --> 00:07:24,873
Some keep very quiet.

108
00:07:24,956 --> 00:07:28,082
Some have already been
absorbed by a cursed spirit.

109
00:07:29,247 --> 00:07:30,665
This is resonance.

110
00:07:32,248 --> 00:07:34,165
Sukuna's finger kept
its power repressed

111
00:07:34,248 --> 00:07:36,999
within the cursed spirit
that had absorbed it.

112
00:07:37,083 --> 00:07:40,415
But back in June, when
Sukuna manifested in Itadori,

113
00:07:40,499 --> 00:07:42,083
it released its cursed energy.

114
00:07:42,749 --> 00:07:44,999
This one looks the same

115
00:07:45,083 --> 00:07:46,883
as the one from the
juvenile detention center,

116
00:07:46,916 --> 00:07:50,540
but it's probably
several degrees

117
00:07:50,624 --> 00:07:51,624
(gasp)

118
00:07:53,248 --> 00:07:54,248
(grunt)

119
00:07:55,832 --> 00:07:57,624
stronger!

120
00:08:03,248 --> 00:08:04,248
(chuckle)

121
00:08:08,290 --> 00:08:09,332
Nue!

122
00:08:14,665 --> 00:08:15,582
Aah.

123
00:08:15,665 --> 00:08:16,916
Guess I win again.

124
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:20,582
This is unusual.

125
00:08:20,665 --> 00:08:23,582
You rarely ask me
to train you, Megumi.

126
00:08:23,665 --> 00:08:25,665
Are you trying to
catch back up to Yuji?

127
00:08:26,957 --> 00:08:30,624
Well, I guess beggars
can't be choosers.

128
00:08:30,707 --> 00:08:32,415
It really bothers you that much?

129
00:08:32,499 --> 00:08:33,499
To ask me for help?

130
00:08:33,957 --> 00:08:36,207
Listen, Megumi.

131
00:08:36,290 --> 00:08:38,415
I think you have
just as much ability

132
00:08:38,499 --> 00:08:40,291
and potential as Yuji does.

133
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:44,416
The only thing holding
you back is your mindset.

134
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:45,500
Megumi.

135
00:08:45,583 --> 00:08:48,084
You don't know how to
bring out your best, do you?

136
00:08:49,333 --> 00:08:50,375
Huh?

137
00:08:50,833 --> 00:08:53,750
Are you saying I haven't
been giving it my best?

138
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:56,958
I'm not saying you
haven't, I'm saying you can't.

139
00:08:57,042 --> 00:08:58,792
For example, in the ball game...

140
00:08:58,875 --> 00:09:02,333
Why did you lay down
that sacrifice bunt?

141
00:09:05,084 --> 00:09:06,458
(grunt)

142
00:09:06,541 --> 00:09:08,125
Was it to advance the runner

143
00:09:08,208 --> 00:09:10,666
even though it meant
that you'd be out?

144
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:12,792
That is good team play.

145
00:09:12,875 --> 00:09:16,000
But Yuji would always go for
a home run, and so would I.

146
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,708
I'm not saying a bunt is bad.

147
00:09:20,792 --> 00:09:23,249
Baseball is a team sport.

148
00:09:23,333 --> 00:09:24,750
And everyone has
their role to play.

149
00:09:24,833 --> 00:09:29,625
But jujutsu sorcery
is an individual sport.

150
00:09:29,708 --> 00:09:32,125
Isn't working with the
other sorcerers important?

151
00:09:32,875 --> 00:09:34,625
Of course.

152
00:09:34,708 --> 00:09:37,375
But no matter how many
allies you have around you,

153
00:09:38,208 --> 00:09:39,368
when you die you'll be alone.

154
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:44,708
You can only piece
together undervalued data

155
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:45,917
on yourself and others.

156
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,501
You can't imagine a stronger
future version of yourself.

157
00:09:50,584 --> 00:09:52,834
Maybe that's because
of your trump card?

158
00:09:52,918 --> 00:09:54,709
You believe that
in the worst case,

159
00:09:54,793 --> 00:09:58,292
you can resolve everything
at the cost of your life.

160
00:09:58,376 --> 00:10:01,334
But at that point,
forget about beating me.

161
00:10:01,417 --> 00:10:03,417
You'll never even
measure up to Nanami.

162
00:10:03,876 --> 00:10:06,918
Dying to win and
risking death to win,

163
00:10:09,918 --> 00:10:12,376
are completely
different, Megumi.

164
00:10:15,793 --> 00:10:17,334
Give it your best.

165
00:10:17,417 --> 00:10:18,459
Be greedier.

166
00:10:29,292 --> 00:10:31,501
How many seconds
was I unconscious?

167
00:10:32,793 --> 00:10:34,001
My Demon Dog's destroyed.

168
00:10:34,834 --> 00:10:37,001
No, the technique was released.

169
00:10:37,085 --> 00:10:39,667
(evil cackle)

170
00:10:40,793 --> 00:10:44,417
So I guess, this is it for me.

171
00:10:45,001 --> 00:10:47,043
Sacred treasure!

172
00:10:48,626 --> 00:10:50,250
Sacred swing!

173
00:10:55,292 --> 00:10:56,209
Hmph.

174
00:10:56,292 --> 00:10:58,627
Kind of a waste of your talents.

175
00:10:59,794 --> 00:11:02,002
(light chuckle)

176
00:11:02,086 --> 00:11:03,627
Oh what the hell?

177
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:06,919
A jujutsu sorcerer's
growth curve

178
00:11:07,002 --> 00:11:10,460
isn't necessarily
a gentle slope.

179
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:14,044
One thing I don't get.

180
00:11:14,127 --> 00:11:15,207
Why did you run, back then?

181
00:11:17,002 --> 00:11:19,460
Spit out the entire
depths of my shadow.

182
00:11:20,710 --> 00:11:23,335
Worry about a
specific structure later.

183
00:11:24,835 --> 00:11:27,668
Just push it out as soon as
I collect the cursed energy.

184
00:11:28,086 --> 00:11:31,418
Imagine a future
version of myself,

185
00:11:31,502 --> 00:11:34,044
who's freely
surpassed my limits!

186
00:11:34,127 --> 00:11:35,710
Oh I can do that!

187
00:11:36,710 --> 00:11:38,418
[Gojo] With a strong foundation

188
00:11:38,502 --> 00:11:40,020
and a little bit of
sense and imagination,

189
00:11:40,044 --> 00:11:44,543
it just takes the slightest
trigger to change a person.

190
00:11:46,002 --> 00:11:47,002
Domain Expansion:

191
00:11:53,377 --> 00:11:55,543
Chimera Shadow Garden!

192
00:11:59,086 --> 00:11:59,919
It's incomplete!

193
00:12:00,002 --> 00:12:03,210
And it's ugly work at best!

194
00:12:03,293 --> 00:12:05,377
But for now, that's fine!

195
00:12:21,503 --> 00:12:22,503
Broaden it

196
00:12:25,003 --> 00:12:26,961
more freely!

197
00:12:30,544 --> 00:12:31,920
The interpretation

198
00:12:34,586 --> 00:12:35,920
of the technique!

199
00:12:36,586 --> 00:12:38,003
(lightning strikes)

200
00:12:40,586 --> 00:12:44,336
(intense music)

201
00:12:44,419 --> 00:12:46,045
(rising roar)

202
00:12:53,586 --> 00:12:55,753
(giggle)

203
00:12:59,128 --> 00:13:01,920
Demon Dog Totality's claws

204
00:13:03,087 --> 00:13:04,327
were able to injure that thing.

205
00:13:08,586 --> 00:13:10,461
So they'd have no trouble
piercing through you

206
00:13:10,544 --> 00:13:12,169
when you're caught off-guard.

207
00:13:24,046 --> 00:13:25,046
I'm tired.

208
00:13:28,962 --> 00:13:30,712
Now, for the other guys.

209
00:13:30,796 --> 00:13:31,796
Where'd they go?

210
00:13:35,587 --> 00:13:36,587
Good!

211
00:13:36,670 --> 00:13:38,004
That's very good!

212
00:13:40,462 --> 00:13:42,670
(retching)

213
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:55,670
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

214
00:13:59,379 --> 00:14:00,837
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

215
00:14:05,004 --> 00:14:08,212
There's one fundamental
rule for interacting with others.

216
00:14:08,295 --> 00:14:09,712
You know what that is?

217
00:14:11,004 --> 00:14:12,046
[Bully] No I don't.

218
00:14:12,129 --> 00:14:13,129
It's simple.

219
00:14:14,129 --> 00:14:16,088
It's "I won't kill you,

220
00:14:16,170 --> 00:14:19,379
"so in return please
don't kill me either."

221
00:14:19,462 --> 00:14:21,212
Substitute any word for "kill".

222
00:14:21,295 --> 00:14:23,587
The point is drawing a line

223
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:25,022
so you don't
infringe on the other.

224
00:14:25,046 --> 00:14:27,797
In order for both
to exist together

225
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,005
they need to honor that.

226
00:14:30,421 --> 00:14:32,797
Just strutting around
breaking that rule,

227
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,963
so that others have to
try not to piss you off

228
00:14:35,047 --> 00:14:37,089
must have made
you feel powerful,

229
00:14:39,338 --> 00:14:42,463
Next time you do it
around me, I'll kill you.

230
00:14:42,546 --> 00:14:45,089
Yeah but, what did
we ever do to you?

231
00:14:45,171 --> 00:14:48,797
Figure it out yourself or die.

232
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:49,880
[Takeda] Hey you!

233
00:14:50,963 --> 00:14:54,588
T-T-T-T-Today I tell off
Ikezawa and his gang!

234
00:14:54,671 --> 00:14:56,230
I'm not gonna be their
stupid gofer anymore!

235
00:14:56,254 --> 00:14:58,005
Yeah you tell 'em

236
00:14:58,089 --> 00:14:59,005
Do it!

237
00:14:59,089 --> 00:15:00,005
Oh but Aida,

238
00:15:00,089 --> 00:15:02,005
that's just gonna make
me their next target!

239
00:15:02,089 --> 00:15:04,588
So do me a favor
and don't try too hard!

240
00:15:04,671 --> 00:15:06,338
Oh not a chance fatty!

241
00:15:06,421 --> 00:15:07,797
I'm done messing around!

242
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:09,065
Starting today,
I'm gonna tell 'em

243
00:15:09,089 --> 00:15:10,963
you're my new replacement!

244
00:15:11,047 --> 00:15:12,230
Dude, you'd sell
out your best friend?

245
00:15:12,254 --> 00:15:14,755
You're damn right I would!

246
00:15:15,089 --> 00:15:16,130
[Tsumiki] Megumi.

247
00:15:19,296 --> 00:15:20,380
Hey, look!

248
00:15:20,463 --> 00:15:24,171
Isn't that Ikezawa and his
buddies piled up over there?

249
00:15:24,254 --> 00:15:26,338
You told me you
wouldn't fight anymore.

250
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:28,500
Yeah well you're not my mom.

251
00:15:30,296 --> 00:15:32,171
I hate bad people.

252
00:15:36,714 --> 00:15:38,048
They act so damn superior

253
00:15:38,131 --> 00:15:40,672
when their empathy
and imagination

254
00:15:40,756 --> 00:15:42,090
are as empty as a vacant lot.

255
00:15:42,172 --> 00:15:45,506
I can't deal with
good people either.

256
00:15:45,589 --> 00:15:47,714
Because they forgive
those bad people.

257
00:15:48,131 --> 00:15:51,131
And they view the act of
forgiveness as a noble thing.

258
00:15:52,923 --> 00:15:53,923
Makes me want to vomit.

259
00:15:56,714 --> 00:15:59,798
Tsumiki's a perfect
example of a good person.

260
00:16:00,631 --> 00:16:01,756
I detest you.

261
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:07,672
Agh! Sorry!

262
00:16:07,756 --> 00:16:09,381
I didn't think it
would come out!

263
00:16:11,297 --> 00:16:13,422
When I was in first grade

264
00:16:13,506 --> 00:16:15,255
my father and Tsumiki's mother,

265
00:16:15,339 --> 00:16:17,631
the two of them hooked up,

266
00:16:18,631 --> 00:16:20,339
and vanished without a trace.

267
00:16:23,172 --> 00:16:25,339
A suspicious
white-haired man told us...

268
00:16:25,422 --> 00:16:27,714
The thing about your dad...

269
00:16:27,798 --> 00:16:30,255
He's from a big clan
among the jujutsu sorcerers

270
00:16:30,339 --> 00:16:31,881
called the Zen'in.

271
00:16:31,964 --> 00:16:34,214
They're so inept
even I'm freaked out.

272
00:16:34,297 --> 00:16:36,964
Your father left the
clan in order to have you.

273
00:16:38,048 --> 00:16:38,923
Megumi.

274
00:16:39,006 --> 00:16:41,589
Your father was saving
you as the ultimate card

275
00:16:41,672 --> 00:16:43,923
to use against the Zen'in clan.

276
00:16:44,006 --> 00:16:45,215
Pisses you off, huh?

277
00:16:47,382 --> 00:16:49,298
That solved the mystery

278
00:16:49,382 --> 00:16:51,590
of how they got enough
money to disappear.

279
00:16:51,673 --> 00:16:54,215
Apparently, I had been
sold to that Zen'in clan.

280
00:16:54,465 --> 00:16:57,382
And yeah, it pissed me off.

281
00:16:57,465 --> 00:16:59,382
Especially his lack
of tact about it.

282
00:16:59,465 --> 00:17:04,465
And that irritating guy stopped
my sale to the Zen'in clan.

283
00:17:04,548 --> 00:17:06,382
And used the promise
that I would work

284
00:17:06,465 --> 00:17:09,298
as a jujutsu
sorcerer as collateral

285
00:17:09,382 --> 00:17:11,924
in order to get financial
aid from Jujutsu High

286
00:17:12,007 --> 00:17:13,007
to support us both.

287
00:17:15,465 --> 00:17:17,132
What's this jujutsu
sorcerer crap, anyway?

288
00:17:17,215 --> 00:17:19,507
It's bullshit.

289
00:17:19,590 --> 00:17:21,548
Who the hell would I ever save?

290
00:17:21,632 --> 00:17:22,965
Hey, Tsumiki!

291
00:17:23,049 --> 00:17:24,965
What the hell do you
think you're doing?

292
00:17:25,049 --> 00:17:26,049
Hi Megumi!

293
00:17:27,049 --> 00:17:27,965
Oh nothing.

294
00:17:28,049 --> 00:17:28,965
Hey, hold on.

295
00:17:29,049 --> 00:17:30,965
Did you give any thought
to the test of courage

296
00:17:31,049 --> 00:17:32,548
I was telling you about?

297
00:17:32,632 --> 00:17:34,007
I don't want to do it,

298
00:17:34,091 --> 00:17:36,382
but I'll go because
I'm worried about you.

299
00:17:36,465 --> 00:17:39,882
Shortly after I started ninth
grade, Tsumiki was cursed.

300
00:17:41,215 --> 00:17:42,799
The identity was unknown.

301
00:17:42,882 --> 00:17:44,340
The origin was unknown.

302
00:17:44,423 --> 00:17:48,007
But there were several victims
of the same curse nationwide.

303
00:17:48,091 --> 00:17:51,132
All I found out was that
nobody knew anything.

304
00:17:51,215 --> 00:17:53,966
And Tsumiki was left in a coma.

305
00:17:54,050 --> 00:17:55,410
If I had the time
to curse someone,

306
00:17:55,466 --> 00:17:58,383
I'd rather spend it
thinking about people I love.

307
00:17:58,466 --> 00:18:03,008
She always smiled and
spouted noble ideals.

308
00:18:03,092 --> 00:18:05,841
Not forgiving people
isn't such a bad thing.

309
00:18:05,925 --> 00:18:07,925
It just goes along
with your kindness.

310
00:18:09,174 --> 00:18:11,341
She even accepted
my strange disposition.

311
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:14,442
Yet Tsumiki would
get genuinely angry

312
00:18:14,466 --> 00:18:16,508
whenever I hurt someone.

313
00:18:17,466 --> 00:18:19,383
And that irritated me,

314
00:18:19,466 --> 00:18:22,008
because I thought
it was hypocritical

315
00:18:22,092 --> 00:18:23,612
in light of her
leave-others-be policy.

316
00:18:24,549 --> 00:18:28,341
But now I realize I
had the wrong idea.

317
00:18:29,925 --> 00:18:31,966
Just as I choose who I save,

318
00:18:33,133 --> 00:18:34,493
she was choosing
me to worry about.

319
00:18:35,466 --> 00:18:36,383
I'm sorry!

320
00:18:36,466 --> 00:18:38,966
I was just a kid!

321
00:18:40,257 --> 00:18:41,257
I apologize!

322
00:18:42,758 --> 00:18:46,383
So wake up already
my stupid sister!

323
00:18:47,424 --> 00:18:50,133
Damn my head hurts!

324
00:18:51,133 --> 00:18:52,591
This Yasohachi Bridge curse

325
00:18:52,674 --> 00:18:54,883
was just overlapping
the other one.

326
00:18:54,966 --> 00:18:58,383
I doubt the curse that put
Tsumiki into a coma was undone.

327
00:18:58,466 --> 00:19:00,383
Now I just have to tell Itadori

328
00:19:01,466 --> 00:19:03,425
the news about
Sukuna's finger, but...

329
00:19:04,425 --> 00:19:05,425
How?

330
00:19:10,175 --> 00:19:11,342
"Fushiguro Fell Asleep"

331
00:19:11,425 --> 00:19:14,258
(shock gasps)

332
00:19:14,342 --> 00:19:16,342
A huge presence just
suddenly appeared.

333
00:19:16,425 --> 00:19:19,509
Has Sukuna's finger
left the barrier?

334
00:19:21,134 --> 00:19:24,217
If a sorcerer exorcised
the finger's host,

335
00:19:24,592 --> 00:19:27,009
they're quite good.

336
00:19:28,175 --> 00:19:30,093
But even if the
others have the finger,

337
00:19:30,175 --> 00:19:32,967
and even if the special-grade
cursed spirit was defeated,

338
00:19:34,175 --> 00:19:35,610
they wouldn't have
come out unscathed.

339
00:19:35,634 --> 00:19:36,967
I hope they're okay.

340
00:19:39,467 --> 00:19:42,093
Actually, on second thought,

341
00:19:42,175 --> 00:19:44,258
please forget
everything I just said.

342
00:19:45,342 --> 00:19:47,093
Hold it right there!

343
00:19:47,175 --> 00:19:48,842
Damn, he's going
after the finger!

344
00:19:50,175 --> 00:19:52,258
You think you can mock me?

345
00:19:52,342 --> 00:19:54,592
Dancing around like
that and still getting away?

346
00:19:55,842 --> 00:19:58,258
The thing is I'm a bit
insecure about my back

347
00:19:58,342 --> 00:20:00,258
so it's only fair
that I warn you.

348
00:20:00,342 --> 00:20:02,134
If you see my back,
I'll be forced to ki--

349
00:20:02,217 --> 00:20:02,550
Oh!

350
00:20:02,634 --> 00:20:04,884
Kugisaki!

351
00:20:04,967 --> 00:20:05,967
Oh here you are, brother!

352
00:20:11,051 --> 00:20:13,468
(screams)

353
00:20:13,551 --> 00:20:14,611
-What the hell is that?
-Oh I'm sorry brother!

354
00:20:14,635 --> 00:20:17,760
It wasn't on purpose! I
didn't mean to see that!

355
00:20:17,843 --> 00:20:18,843
Now I have to kill you!

356
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,551
That must be the
source of that weird smell.

357
00:20:27,635 --> 00:20:30,301
Why don't you just cover it up?

358
00:20:30,385 --> 00:20:32,760
'Cause then it gets musty!

359
00:20:32,843 --> 00:20:33,343
Rot Technique!

360
00:20:33,426 --> 00:20:34,468
Supreme Art!

361
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:39,802
Wing King!

362
00:20:41,426 --> 00:20:43,635
Death by Wasp!

363
00:20:45,426 --> 00:20:48,593
(ending theme music)

364
00:20:55,885 --> 00:20:59,885
(singing in Japanese)

365
00:22:15,803 --> 00:22:17,719
[Unison] Juju Stroll!

366
00:22:19,344 --> 00:22:20,594
Gojo!

367
00:22:20,677 --> 00:22:22,469
Kugisaki!

368
00:22:22,552 --> 00:22:23,719
(annoyed sigh)

369
00:22:23,803 --> 00:22:26,594
So annoying.

370
00:22:26,677 --> 00:22:29,095
It's way too hot out here
for your nonsense, Itadori.

371
00:22:29,177 --> 00:22:31,428
Fushiguro is getting hit on!

372
00:22:32,804 --> 00:22:34,470
Formation B!

373
00:22:34,553 --> 00:22:35,720
[Unison] Roger that!

374
00:22:37,345 --> 00:22:39,220
[Both] Fushiguro, no!

375
00:22:40,137 --> 00:22:41,595
Who is this woman, Fushiguro?

376
00:22:41,678 --> 00:22:43,428
Don't tell me you've
forgotten that night?

377
00:22:43,512 --> 00:22:44,137
That special night
we had together

378
00:22:44,220 --> 00:22:45,804
when you looked longingly at me

379
00:22:45,887 --> 00:22:48,804
and made that toast to
the beauty of my eyes!

380
00:22:48,887 --> 00:22:51,345
Whoa, what's with you?

381
00:22:52,345 --> 00:22:53,345
Seriously, you two?

382
00:22:53,387 --> 00:22:55,303
Could you please take
your hands off him?

383
00:22:55,387 --> 00:22:57,137
You homewreckers!

384
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:59,637
Megumi has violin
practice with me now.

385
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,760
Let's get you back home,
Megumi, so you can warm up.

386
00:23:02,762 --> 00:23:04,595
Today I think we'll
try something new,

387
00:23:04,678 --> 00:23:08,762
and I'll have you master
"Twinkle Twinkle Little Star."

388
00:23:09,762 --> 00:23:11,553
It's okay, don't mind them.

389
00:23:11,637 --> 00:23:12,970
The station's straight ahead.

390
00:23:13,054 --> 00:23:13,970
Just go that way.

391
00:23:14,054 --> 00:23:15,553
Thank you so much.

392
00:23:15,637 --> 00:23:17,470
[Unison] Huh?

393
00:23:17,553 --> 00:23:19,970
Okay, seriously, what's up?

394
00:23:20,054 --> 00:23:22,012
You three are totally
embarrassing me.

395
00:23:25,595 --> 00:23:27,303
Stop doing that!

396
00:23:27,387 --> 00:23:29,970
(embarrassed laugh)

397
00:23:30,054 --> 00:23:32,595
(upbeat music)

398
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:39,887
"Episode 24: The Origin
of Blind Obedience"

